+++ b/FIXED-METADATA-SLICE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+# RootHealth fixed-system data slice (fail-closed rebase proposal)
+
+This isolated slice implements bounded, data-only candidates for WAL action 20
+(`$UpCase`) and action 21 (`$AttrDef`).  It is not a production authorization.
+The stable fixed check IDs are `system.upcase` and `system.attrdef`.
+`roothealth_policy.c` deliberately still has no implementation entry for
+`PR_UPCASE_CORRUPTED` or `PR_ATTRDEF_CORRUPTED`, and the tests require that gate
+to remain closed.
+
+## Canonical inputs
+
+- `$UpCase` is built by the pinned ntfs-next `d4f481d`
+  `ntfs_upcase_build_default()` routine.  The result must be exactly 131072
+  bytes and SHA-256
+  `41c26bc7a12bdaeb26025c93118697c7e3ef81ee048b00fe5cce2a472e0e0742`.
+- `$AttrDef` is copied from the pinned `attrdef_ntfs3x_array` asset.  The result
+  must be exactly 2560 bytes and SHA-256
+  `d7de5b1b2f79f45f235ceb1adbc46908ed64eae174eb90ed66aefe5f25165da3`.
+
+The output hashes are checked every time canonical bytes are built.  A source
+change that produces different bytes is an internal failure, not new repair
+authority.  The pinned source-file SHA-256 values qualified here are
+`1f40ffcf68a0decb95af39d0f3b0663e7378e6bdd8a803afdd56f119c051e625`
+for `libntfs/unistr.c` and
+`27d5fa53b6e63abffa6226f9c46bae867a64919c42c97e216e4f847f13ff9f6b`
+for `src/attrdef.c`.
+
+## Closed predicates
+
+Both actions require a sealed RHCOV3 full-coverage ledger; raw T1OS identity;
+complete MFT, attribute, extent, run and target-ownership censuses; no I/O
+uncertainty; and proof that every target lies outside the internal WAL.
+
+Action 20 additionally requires the complete reciprocal namespace manifest,
+the complete index/block census, and proof that every index is ordered under
+the canonical table.  Action 21 additionally requires a complete attribute
+type-use census, zero custom types, and zero incompatible bounds.  Missing,
+partial, contradictory, or tampered authority is refused before an operation
+is added.
+
+Production authority is constructed only by
+`rh_fixed_metadata_authority_build()`, which cross-checks the release-green
+RHCOV3 denominators against the real raw-MFT, canonical namespace/I30 and
+cluster-allocation censuses.  The old generic counter sealer is compiled only
+into the isolated negative-test binary and is unavailable to production.
+
+The local target parser accepts only fixed record 10 or 4 respectively, a live
+base record with no attribute-list extents, one unnamed nonresident `AT_DATA`,
+the exact release size and allocation, one dense extent with a
+strict zero mapping-pairs tail, and the supported geometry.  Size changes,
+allocation changes, missing attributes and extent reconstruction are outside
+this data-only slice.
+
+## Planning and recovery
+
+Both fixed targets form one exact bounded batch.  RootHealth first uses
+`ntfs_volume_startup()` through its private read-only overlay to load only the
+boot metadata and `$MFT`.  It captures and hashes the raw streams for records
+10 and 4 before either corrupt table can control a full mount.  Each target is
+then recorded as clean or planned; only after both have been examined does one
+ordinary read-only/forensic/no-repair full mount run over the staged writer
+view.  There is no libntfs source or ordinary-mount behavior change.  If the
+second target refuses or errors after the first was clean or planned, the
+batch is discarded to its original checkpoint, both examined bits are
+cleared, and no partial plan is returned.
+
+One exact whole-stream operation is emitted for each corrupt table; fragment
+or changed-range repair is forbidden.  Each write goes through
+`rh_ntfs_overlay_run_action()` and receives an exact typed nonresident target:
+record/sequence, attribute instance/type/name hash, lowest/logical VCN, LCN,
+logical range and physical range.  The overlay performs its mandatory fresh
+forensic remount.  A separately sealed staged-view ledger must then prove the
+canonical stream, unchanged mapping and complete final view before the targets
+can be finalized for WAL serialization.  Planning and finalization perform no
+target write.
+
+Crash rederivation accepts the WAL descriptor fields plus two read-only views.
+The pre-transaction view is reconstructed from undo bytes.  The staged view is
+the current device for `COMMITTED`, or a virtual canonical overlay for
+`PREPARING`/`APPLYING`.  It reruns both authorities, reparses the exact fixed
+stream, reconstructs the complete changed-slice set, and reproduces every
+target, old/new/semantic hash, evidence seal and staged-view seal.  Retargeted
+offset/LCN, content hash, size, attribute name, owner record, evidence hash and
+staged-view hash variants are rejected.
+
+## Qualification and remaining integration gates
+
+Run `tests/roothealth_fixed_metadata_qualification.sh`.  It checks the two
+canonical artifacts, clean no-op paths, tail and parser-breaking corruptions,
+the UpCase-only, AttrDef-only and both-corrupt matrices, unchanged ordinary
+mount semantics, whole-image no-write probes, absent/tampered/incomplete
+census refusal, both first-clean/second-refused and
+first-corrupt/second-refused atomic aborts, fresh remount convergence,
+PREPARING and COMMITTED rederivation, descriptor negative matrices, strict
+`-Werror`, and ASan/UBSan.
+
+The rebased proposal remains deliberately fail-closed.  The complete checker
+does not yet publish a production RHCOV3 fixed-system authority object, and
+the approved WAL registry has no ID20/21 callback capable of rebuilding the
+full raw/namespace/type-use/allocation evidence from its opaque virtual
+preimage.  Consequently ID20/21 are not registered and central policy remains
+closed.  Both must stay closed until a source-bound rederiver and real outer
+ledger producer land together; digest comparison or injected synthetic
+authority is not an acceptable recovery substitute.
